    {
      "id": "59044ce1-5ef7-44c7-a78b-ad3372390c0b",
      "sentence": "Athens filled every office of state by sortition, with one exception: the generals, who were elected.",
      "blurb": "Sortition means drawing names by lot. No office required any qualification, so any citizen could end up holding one. Military command was the single job where expertise was not left to chance.",
      "quote": {
        "text": "…lot determined all offices of state, apart from the generalship, which was decided on popular vote. It literally takes my breath away, this astounding faith in every man.",
        "timestamp": "00:31:01"
      },
      "transcriptRef": "transcripts/01-why-athenian-democracy-matters.md [00:06:00, 00:31:01]",
